{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"8716411663006e8c","x":-920,"y":802,"width":1910,"height":1280,"type":"group","label":"idk where"},
		{"id":"0f2c04db7525549a","x":1363,"y":875,"width":2117,"height":1149,"type":"group","label":"Cut?"},
		{"id":"3421c557d0861f88","x":-849,"y":2252,"width":1928,"height":1217,"type":"group","label":"Worldbuilding Notes"},
		{"id":"aef96932d605874f","x":-460,"y":-120,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"\"Sometimes, it's almost like I can still fell her.\" Sara said. \"Is that even possible?\"\n\n\"I have been told that some spirits do linger.\" Lilith said. \n\n\"Is there some way to know if it's Emma?\" What Sara has felt was so faint, like whisper so soft she wasn't even sure if she'd heard anything at all. "},
		{"id":"60dac33c79db70c9","x":-720,"y":2400,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Idk, might cut this:\n\nAnne is also more like to show that she can feel Emma. Sara is more likely to brush it off and seem like nothing Emma is doing is getting through to her. Emma cannot \"sense\" or \"feel\" if what she did got through, she cannot mind read. Emma as a spirit can only watch and observe, so she only knows if an attempt at communication works if the other person does or says something that makes it clear that it worked. If Sara just takes a deep breath to center herself, then Emma can't be sure Sara felt what Emma did. But if Anne rolls her eyes, looks up, and says \"Emma I'm trying to do my homework right now\" or something like that, then Emma knows it was effective/successful. "},
		{"id":"36e9c91aa1d406db","x":-160,"y":2400,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Anne is not a fully developed vampire, because she was sort of turned in utero. She isn't a true born vampire, she was human at conception. But she isn't a true turned vampire either, because she wasn't bitten. She is something else. As a child she lacks multiple vampire abilities/attributes; she doesn't have fangs for example. But Anne does have at least some of a connection to the darkness, she has vampire senses. \n\nAt least to some degree. Idk if Anne is average or slight above average. Though Sara is way way way above average, so Sara will be able to better feel those faint occasional hints at Emma's spirit. "},
		{"id":"c72eb23cd3ccbc6d","x":-760,"y":1000,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"\"Well, whatever it is, I don't think any part of this is supposed to be easy.\" Don knew how much Sara loved her kids. \"You tired of being told I'm sorry yet?\" \n\nSara sighed, that one didn't bother her so much. \"Eh. I know people mean well when they say it.\" Heck knew she'd probably said it too many times to Jane. She just didn't know what else to say. Made sense that other people didn't either. "},
		{"id":"73df07a87662c210","x":120,"y":1160,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Normally on a night off at this time, Sara would be curled up with Jane. But, from what Sara could tell, Jane was sleeping more than she had since becoming a vampire, while Sara herself was sleeping even less. So Jane was still sleeping, but at least Jane didn't seem to be having nightmares anymore.\n\nAt first she's been spending the nights with Jane, but now Jane's nightmares had stopped. She'd said she was fine sleeping alone, and not to worry about her. From what Sara could tell, Jane was sleeping more than she had since becoming a vampire, while Sara herself was sleeping even less."},
		{"id":"d002922cad4a2dc5","x":520,"y":1160,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Especially during the first few nights, Sara had stayed in their bedroom whenever Jane slept. Sara hadn't had any dream or nightmares about Emma yet, if anything she found that kind of odd, but maybe they would come later for her. From what Sara could tell, it seemed like Jane was sleep more and she was sleeping less. It left her with too much time to think. "},
		{"id":"a11e3895be138d6e","x":1560,"y":1080,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"\n\"What's with the extra plate?\" Sara asked. \n\n\"I didn't know if Emma would want some, so I got her a plate too.\" \n\nSavanna looked scared as she blinked away tears. \n\nSara came over to her, \"Do you want a hug sweetie?\"\n\nSavanna shook her head for no, then got up and went back to her room. \n\nSara frowned, Savanna had spent a lot of time in her room lately. Sara and Jane had both been checking on her from time to time, but she always wanted to be left alone. \n\n\"Hey Anne,\" How to phrase this to not upset her? Sara searched for the words. \"Do we have to put out a plate for Emma?\"\n\n\"I don't know, she won't tell me.\" Anne shrugged. \"I'm not sure she knows if she needs it.\" \n\n\"Ok.\" Sara swallowed, \"well, maybe could we try not setting one out at least when Savanna is around?\" \n\n\"I guess we can try it, at least for a little while.\" \n\n----\n\nSara felt tears well up in her eyes as she looked at Emma's urn. Would is ever feel like Emma wasn't here in the house with them? Sometimes it hurt that it felt like that, but Sara honestly wasn't sure if she even wanted that feeling to stop. It was like she could sense Emma, similar to how Sara could sense Anne near her. \n\n\"What is it Momma?\" Anne said from the doorway to Emma's room.\n\nSara wiped her eyes, \"I just get sad sometimes because Emma is gone.\" It was easier to be open when it was modeling healthy emotions for her girls. \n\n\"But Emma isn't gone.\" Anne looked at the urn as she came over near it too. \"She didn't leave, she just changed.\" Anne turned to look up at Sara, \"I thought you felt her too?\"\n\nSara didn't even know how to respond. Thankfully, Jane called for her. "},
		{"id":"d2699b263f415cc6","x":2240,"y":1240,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"There are multiple moments where Anne just casually acts & talks as if Emma is still around. At least in some way. She doesn't seem disconnected with reality or in denial. Maybe even at some points, one of the adults are like Emma is dead, and Anne is like well yeah but she's not gone. Anne knows Emma has an urn, but Anne can also feel that 'Emma is still here just different'\n\nMaybe Sara is talking to Lilith at some point, because they do regularly hang out / see each other, often with Don there. And Sara is talking about how it's weird because Anne talks like she's in denial but doesn't seem to be in denial. \n\nSo during one of their outing, Sara just ends up alone with Lilith, and Lilith asks her how she's doing. \n\nSara sighed, \"I don't mean to be rude but that one has more than gotten old.\" \n\nLilith waited patiently.\n\n\"I'm fine. I'm hanging in there. I have good days and bad days. Honestly I'm more worried about Anne than anyone should be about me.\"\n\n\"What's going on with Anne?\"\n\n----\n\nOr maybe like Lilith approaches Sara while she's alone or something like that and asks how everyone is doing, how her family is doing. And it's refreshing in a way to have someone not ask about how Sara is doing. Or like Lilith asks what has been going on with her lately, not how she's feeling, but just if there's anything new going on. \n\nSara rubbed her face, \"Nothing about this child will ever be simple I guess.\" The pregnancy has certain been complex to say the least, and Sara supposed she shouldn't have expected things to change now. Anne had never been straight forward. Though complex seemed to be the rule when it came to kids, no matter their species. \n\nLilith rubbed her fingers, \"I would not be so hasty to dismiss the young vampire.\" she paused. \"While perhaps she is not facing the true reality of the situation, there is a chance she is.\" Lilith looked to Sara, \"I am unsure how much you recall, but on that day at the pool, I believe she could sense what had occurred without being having seen or being told of it. Savanna was assuredly in denial about the situation at first, though Anne was not to the point that they argued about it. Without me having told Anne anything of what happened.\" \n\n\"Wait a sec, if Anne didn't see it, then who told Anne what happened? To me it seemed like everyone already knew what I got to your house.\" Don said. \n\nEveryone went quiet. Sara looked around the table, \"So who told her then?\"\n\nDon shook his head.\n\n\"I do not.\" Lilith said. \"And to my knowledge, neither did Jane. She didn't say much at all before I went to my own home.\"\n\nLilith spoke again, \"You have said before that you still feel as though Emma is nearby when you are within your home. I wonder if that feeling is true. I cannot know, you have to decide that yourself.\" \n\n----\n\nOr maybe they do another like family outing, like someone where the kids come with, and Jane & Don are with Savanna and Anne, while Lilith is with Sara, and Lilith asks how they are doing, guestering at Sara's family. \n\n\"I'm honestly not sure. I think Jane is getting better, well, though she's still sleeping a lot. Savanna almost never comes out of her room. And Anne I think is in a weird form of denial. I don't know. She talks like as if Emma is around us sometimes.\" \n\nOr maybe Sara does go to Lilith, to ask. Because well maybe she fears that like she'll sound crazy or something, she can't shake that feeling her daughter says you know don't you feel her too it's just like is that even possible, I mean you know years ago I would have said no but I'm a vampire who lost a gamble to the grim reaper. A few years back I would have said that was impossible too. "},
		{"id":"6e2c561e227a582a","x":2800,"y":1440,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"\nWhich puts Sara in this place where she knows what it sounds like and she knows what it looks like, but because of what it feels like she can't give up this quest. Because if there's even a small chance she is feeling Emma, then not pursuing this would be abandoning her daughter when she needs Sara the most. I mean Sara isn't going to be reckless about this, and like bankrupt the family or anything that, she still fully wants to protect the living members of her family, but she can't give up on this and just ignore her vampire senses telling her Emma is there and sometimes that Emma is sad or happy or whatever Emma sends her. \n"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}